sh;DREAMS III): study design and research methodology</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">.<span class=\"apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><span class=\"ref-journal\">BMC Ophthalmol</span><span class=\"apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>2011;<span class=\"ref-vol\">11</span>:7</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;&#10;margin-left:.25in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in;&#10;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&#10;Arial\">10.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Sateesh Pujari and Estari Mamidala (2015). Anti-diabetic activity of Physagulin-F isolated from Physalis angulata fruits. The American Journal of Science and Medical Research, 2015,1(2):53-60. doi:10.17812/ajsmr2015113...<o:p></o:p></span></p>', 'Cataract, Type 2 Diabetes mellitus, Adilabad, Lens, capsular.', 'Chintala Priyanka and Estari Mamidala (2015). Incidence of cataract in type 2 diabetes mellitus among Rural people. The American Journal of Science and Medical Research, 1(4):108-111. doi:10.17812/ajsmr2015141  Received 2 September 2015; Accepted 18 October, 2015 Published online  20 October, 2015', 'Received: 2 September 2015; Accepted: 18 October 2015; Published: 20 October 2015', 1),
(32, 'A study on the severity of right ventricular dysfunction in correlation with the severity of Lung dysfunction in Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease patients - COPD', 'Original Research Article I Volume 1 I Issue 4 I 2015', 'D. Radha Krishnan and Barama Srihari', 'American Journal of Science and Medical Research; 1(4); 112-119', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr2015142', '../pdffiles/cimg101846_11.20 RADHAKRISHNA 112-119 f.pdf', 'Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) is characterized by airflow limitation that is not fully reversible. COPD is a powerful and independent risk factor for cardiovascular morbidity and mortality which includes right ventricular (RV) dysfunction and corpulmonale secondary to pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH), coronary artery disease (CAD), and cardiac arrhythmias. The aim of this study is to assess RV dysfunction by utilizing RV parameters obtained by clinical methods, electrocardiography (ECG), and echocardiography and to correlate with the severity of airflow limitation in COPD patients.', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;&#10;margin-left:.25in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in;&#10;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;;\">1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;;\">Global Initiative for Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease &mdash; Global Strategy for Diagnosis, Management, and Prevention of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary disease. http.//www.goldcopd.com.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;&#10;margin-left:.25in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in;&#10;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;;\">2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;;\">M. A. Higham, D. Dawson, J. Joshi, P. Nihoyanno&nbsp; Paulos, N W Morell. Utility of echocardiography in assessment of pulmonary hypertension secondary to COPD. Eur. Respir. J. 2001; 17 1350-355. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;&#10;margin-left:.25in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in;&#10;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;;\">3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;;\">Benjamin Burrows, Louis J. Kettel, Albert H. Niden, Murray Rabinowitz, Carl F . Diener Pattems of Cardiovascular dysufunction in chronic obstructive lung disease. N. Engl J. Med. 1972 ; 286 (17) 