(56, 'Evaluation of Antifungal Activity of substituted Pyrazolones', 'Original Research Article I Volume 3 I Issue 1 I 2017', 'B Lalitha Kumari', 'The American Journal of Science and Medical Research; 2(4) Page 31-34', 'doi:10.17812/ajsmr3101.', '../pdffiles/cimg053743_31.01 jkjagadeeshkumare 1-3.pdf', 'The pyrazoles derivatives are used in the medicinal therapy as anti-bacterials, diuretics, anti-hypertensive, anti-pyretic, analgesics, tranquilizers, anti-inflammatory, anti-convulsion anti-thrombotic, anti- tuberculosis and anti-tumor agents. A large number of pyrazole derivatives viz. 4-arylmethylene-2,4- dihydro-2,5-disubstituted-3H-pyrazol-3-ones; 4,4â€™-arylmethylene bis (2,4- dihydro-2,5-disubstituted-3H-pyrazol-3-ones have got much attention to biological importance.In this paper we discuss about antifungal activity of substituted pyrazoles', '<p>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN\" style=\"text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;; position: relative; top: -3pt;\">1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;;\">K.J. Ryan, C.G. Ray; Medical Microbiology (4<span style=\"position:relative;top:-3.0pt;mso-text-raise:&#10;3.0pt\">th ed.) McGraw Hill 2004.</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:-3.15pt;margin-bottom:&#10;0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:&#10;normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:0in;mso-layout-grid-align:none;&#10;text-autospace:none\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;&#10;fo