-[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"font-size:&#10;10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;&#10;mso-ansi-language:EN\">7.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN\">L.A. Calvo, A.M. Gonzalez-Nogal ; Tetrahedron Lett., 42, pp 8981.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:-3.15pt;margin-bottom:&#10;0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:&#10;-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:0in;mso-layout-grid-align:&#10;none;text-autospace:none\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"font-size:&#10;10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;&#10;mso-ansi-language:EN\">8.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN\">B.A. Bhat, S.C. Puri,&nbsp; G.N. Qazi; Synthetic Commun., 35, pp 1135.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:-3.15pt;margin-bottom:&#10;0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:&#10;-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:0in;mso-layout-grid-align:&#10;none;text-autospace:none\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"font-size:&#10;10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Arial;&#10;mso-ansi-language:EN\">9.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN\">D.C.G.A. Pinto, A.M.S. Silva ; Eur. J. Org. Chem., pp 2593.<o:p></o:p></span></p>', 'Pyrazole, anti-convulsion, anti fungal.', 'Jagadeesh Kumar Ega and Kavitha Siddoju (2017).    Evaluation of Antifungal Activity of substituted Pyrazolones. The Ame J Sci & Med Res, 3(1):1-3. doi:10.17812/ajsmr3101.', 'Received: 25 September 2016; Accepted: 21 November, 2016; Published: 30 December 2016', 1),
(57, 'Evaluation of Antioxidant activity of commonly consumed Fruits of South India', 'Original Research Article I Volume 3 I Issue 1 I 2017', 'Ravulakolanu Vanisree, Madhu Kamarapu, Veenavani Marka and Prameela Devi Yalavarthy', 'American Journal of Science and Medical Research; 3(1); 10-14', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr3103', '../pdffiles/cimg061425_313 prameela 10-14.pdf', 'Consumption of natural foods play important role in preventing health disorders due to oxidative stress caused by free radicals. Fruits are the major ingredients in the Indian diet. However, information on the antioxidant activity of fruits used in Indian diet is inadequate. The main objective of this study is to evaluate the antioxidant activity of some commonly used fruits by Indians such as Manilkara zapota (Sapota), Carica papaya (Papaya), Musa acuminate (Banana) and Psidium guajava (Guava). Antioxidant activity is assessed by DPPH (2,2-diphenyl-1-picryl-hydrazyl) and HRSA (Hydroxyl radical scavenging activity) methods. The present study revealed that the crude methanol extracts of Psidium guajava (Guava) showed the maximum scavenging activity, where as Musa acuminate (Banana) showed minimum scavenging activity in both DPPH method and in HRSA methods.   Scavenging activity of selected fruits revealed that regular usage of Psidium guajava is better than Carica papaya, Manilkara zapota and Musa acuminate in descending order, in the regular Indian diet to overcome the effects of free radicals and be healthy', '<p>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;;\">[1].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><b style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -21.3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;;\">Adam Matkowski and Magdalena Piotrowska,</span></b><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;;\">2006, Antioxidant and free radical&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;scavenging activities of some medicinal plants from the lamiaceae, Fitoterapia., Vol 77(5).,pp:&nbsp; &nbsp; 346-353</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;&#10;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;&#10;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&#10;Arial\">[2].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Carolina Santos, Goreti Botelho, Ilda Caldeira, Am&iacute;lcar Torres and Fernanda M. Ferreira.(2014) Antioxidant activity assessment in fruit liquors and spirits: methods comparison. <i>Journal of Viticulture and Enology</i>, Vol.29(1), pp. 28-34. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;&#10;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;&#10;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&#10;Arial\">[3].<span 