mily:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Schliebs R, Liebmann A, Bhattacharya SK, Kumar A, Ghosal S, Bigl V. Systemic administration of defined extracts from Withania somnifera (Indian Ginseng) and Shilajit differentially affects cholinergic but not glutamatergic and GABAergic markers in rat brain. Neurochem Int. 1997;30(2):181&ndash;90.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;&#10;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;&#10;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&#10;Arial\">[10].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\"> </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Vattem D, Lin YT, Labbe RG, Shetty K: Antimicrobial activity against select food-borne pathogens by phenolic antioxidants enriched in cranberry pomace by solid-state bioprocessing using food grade fungus Rhizopus oligosporus. Process Biochem 2004, 39:1939&ndash;1946...<o:p></o:p></span></p>', 'Antibacterial activity, Withania somnifera, methanol, MIC, agar well diffusion method,', 'Pranavi Sreeramoju and Estari Mamidala (2017).   An Ethnobotanical Survey of Antidiabetic plants used by tribes of Warangal District, Telangana State. The Ame J Sci & Med Res, 3(3):8-11. doi:10.17812/ajsmr3302.', 'Received: 30 May 2017; Accepted: 21 July 2017; Published: 29 July 2017', 1),
(69, 'Effect of Imidacloprid on Glycolytic Enzymes Activity in Fish Channa punctatus', 'Original Research Article I Volume 3 I Issue 3 I 2017', 'T. Venkanna and V. Anil Kumar', 'The American Journal of Science and Medical Research; 3(3); 16-4', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr3304', '../pdffiles/cimg090600_334 venkanna 16-19.pdf', 'In this study the fresh water fish, Channa punctus (Bloch) is exposed to sublethal concentration (0.19ppm) of Imidacloprid for 24hrs, 48hrs, 72hrs and 96hrs exposure periods.  The harmful toxic effect of this chemical is investigated by measuring key enzymes in carbohydrate metabolism.  The investigation on substrates viz., Glycogen, Glucose, Pyruvate and Lactate is done during the exposure period.  The levels of glycogen and pyruvate levels decreased while glucose and the lactate levels increased.  From this data it can be concluded that Imidacloprid has more toxic effect by damaging the tissues at cellular level lead to modulation of the glycolytic enzyme.  So the physiological significance of this toxicity is discussed.', '<p>&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;; font-size: 10pt; text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&#10;Arial\">[1].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Abdul Naveed, Venkateshwarlu P, and Jamiah C., (2004): The action of sublethal concentration of endosulfan and Kelhane on regulation of protein metabolism in the fish, <i>Clarius batrachus</i>, Nat Environ, Pollution, Tech, 3(4), 539-544.<o:p></o:p></span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;&#10;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;&#10;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 21.3pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&#10;Arial\">[2].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Bayne, B.G.I, Widoow and Worral C., (1977): Physiological responses of marine biota to polhtants, Acad Press, New York, U.S.A.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;&#10;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;&#10;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 21.3pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&#10;Arial\">[3].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Butter Worth, K.L., (1972): River Pollution, Cause and Effects, Acad Press, New York, U.S.A.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\