quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:8.5pt;&#10;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">Shirling E.B. and L.D. Gottileb (1966). Methods, classification, identification and discription of genera and species. Vol. 2, The Williams and Wilkins company, Baltimove, 61-292.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:21.3pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:8.5pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[10].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:8.5pt;&#10;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">Swapna Gurrapu and Estari Mamidala (2017). In vitro Antibacterial Activity of Physagulin isolated from Physalis angulata fruits against pathogenic clinically important bacteria. International Journal of Current Research, 9, (08), 55482-55486...<o:p></o:p></span></p>', 'Actinomycetes, antibiotics, coal mines, SCCL.', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr4101 Received : 12 December, 2017 Accepted; 21 January, 2018 Available online : 21 February, 2018', 'Received: 12 December 2017 ; Accepted: 21 January 2018 ; Published: 21 February 2018', 1),
(76, 'Î±-Amylase and Î±-Glucosidase Inhibitory Activity of Physagulin-F Isolated from Physalis angulata Fruits', 'Original Research Article I Volume 4 I Issue 1 I 2017', 'Sateesh Pujari and Estari Mamidala', 'The American Journal Science and Medical Research; 4(1); 6-10', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr4102', '../pdffiles/cimg101152_41.2 sateesh.pujari 6-10.pdf', 'Type 2 diabetes is a chronic medical condition that requires regular monitoring and treatment throughout your life. Natural compounds from plant sources have been extensively used as traditional medicines from centuries. The present study was carried out to isolate and identify the putative antidiabetic compound from the Physalisangulata (PA) fruit. A compound, Physagulin-F was isolated from PA fruit extract. The isolated compound Physagulin-F (50, 75, 100, 150 mg/kg) of Physalisangulata fruit was undertaken to evaluate the inhibitory and anti-diabetic activity against Î±-amylase and Î±-glucosidase. The compound â€˜Physagulin-Fâ€™ showed significant concentration dependent manner antidiabetic activity. The results of this experimental study indicate that isolated compound â€˜Physagulin-Fâ€™, possess anti-diabetic effects against Î±-amylase and Î±-glucosidase enzymes.', '<p>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[1].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">Ahmed, A. B. A., Rao, A. S. and Rao, M. V., In vitro callus and in vivo leaf extract of Gymnemasylvestre stimulate &beta;- cells regeneration and anti-diabetic activity in Wistar rats. Phytomedicine, 2010, 17, 1033&ndash;1039.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;&#10;tab-stops:291.75pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:&#10;9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[2].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">D. Krishna Gopal Rao (2013). Hypoglycemic activity of&nbsp; extracts from Elytrariaacaulis L. Leaves in&nbsp; alloxaninduced diabetic rats. Biolife. 1(1):11-16.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;&#10;tab-stops:291.75pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:&#10;9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[3].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font