ormal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Harborne JB (1 998). Phytochemical methods. A guide to modern techniques of plant analysis.3rd ed., Chapman and Hall Int ed., New York.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;&#10;tab-stops:291.75pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:&#10;9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[9].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Igbinosa, O.O., Igbinosa, E.O., Aiyegoro, O.A (2009). Antimicrobial activity and phytochemical screening of stem bark extracts from Jatrophacuccas (Linn). Afr. J. Phar &amp;Pharmacol, 3: 58-62. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;&#10;tab-stops:291.75pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:&#10;9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[10].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Islam, M. S., Choi, H. and Loots, D. T. L., Effects of dietary onion Allium cepa L. in a high-fat diet streptozotocininduced diabetes rodent model. Ann Nutr. Metab., 2008, 53, 6&ndash;12....<o:p></o:p></span></p>', 'Physalisangulata, Physagulin-F, anti-diabetic, Type 2 diabetes.', ' http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr4102 Received : 12 December 2017 Accepted; 21 January 2018 Available online : 23 February 2018', 'Received: 12 December 2017; Accepted: 21 January 2018 ; Published: 23 February 2018', 1),
(77, 'Prevalence of Overweight and Obesity among Post graduate students, Kakatiya University, Warangal', 'Original Research Article I Volume 4 I Issue 1 I 2018', 'Swapna Gurrapu and Estari Mamidala', 'The American Journal Science and Medical Research; 4(1); 10-14', ' http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr4103', '../pdffiles/cimg110706_41.3 swapnagurrpu 11-14.pdf', 'Throughout the world, obesity & underweight is emerging as a serious problem, not only among adults but also children, teenagers and young adults. Hence, this study was undertaken to find out the prevalence of underweight and overweight among University Hostels. The objective of this study is to assess the prevalence of overweight and obesity among Students of a University Hostels and also to find the relationship of the risk factors like Physical inactivity, sleeping habits, diet, stress and association with other diseases (thyroid disorders, menstrual disorders). A cross-sectional study was conducted in selected sample of 290 subjects. Anthropometric measurements including height and weight were taken as per WHO criteria. Body mass index were calculated and classified accordingly as normal, overweight and obese, normal weight. The study revealed overall a high prevalence of underweight (20%), and overweight (5.5%). In males 3.5% were overweight. While in females 7.3% were overweight and 0.6% were obese. Relation with increased frequency of meals, increased sleep duration and regular exercise were found to be significant.', '<p>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.25in; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[1].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.25in; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">World Health Organization. Obesity: preventing and managing the global epidemic. Report of a WHO Consultation on Obesity, Geneva, 3-5 June 1997. Geneva: World Health Organization; 1998. WHO document WHO/ NUT/NCD/98.1?</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;&#10;tab-stops:291.75pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:&#10;9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[2].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Manojan KK, Benny PV, Anil Bindu. Prevalence of obesity and overweight among medical students based on New Asia-Pacifc BMI guideline.&nbsp; 2014, IPTM Volume 1.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;&#10;tab-stops:291.75pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:&#10;9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[3].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Selvaraj K, Sivaprakasam P. A study on the prevalence of overweight and obesity among medical students of Kanchipuram district. NJRCM 2013; 2(2):140-4.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;&#10;tab-stops:291.75pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:&#10;9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[4].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Gopalakrishnan S, Ganeshkumar P, Prakash MV, Christopher, Amalraj V. Prevalence of overweight/obesity among the medical students, Malaysia. Med J Malaysia. 2012; 67 (4):442-4.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;&#10;tab-stops:291.75pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:&#10;9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[5].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Bertsias G, Mammas I, Linardakis M, Kafatos A. Overweight and obesity in relation to cardio-vascular disease risk factors among medical students in Crete. BMC Public Health 2003;3:3...<o:p></o:p></span></p>', 'Overweight, Obesity, Kakatiya University, WHO', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr4103 Received : 18 December 2017 Accepted; 25 January 2018 Available online : 24 February 2018', 'Received: 18 December 2017 ; Accepted: 25 January 2018 ; Published: 24 February 2018', 1);
INSERT INTO `ajsmr_abstracts` (`contentid`, `conttitle`, `issuedetails`, `authors`, `journal`, `doi`, `abstract`, `abstractsdesc`, `referencestxt`, `keywords`, `howtoguide`, `articledates`, `status`) VALUES
(78, 'Seaweeds and Itâ€™s Utility', 'Original Research Article I Volume 4 I Issue 1 I 2018', 'S. Kameswaran', 'The American Journal Science and Medical Research; 4(1); 15-19', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr4104', '../pdffiles/cimg111222_41.4 kambharath 15-19.pdf', 'The unprecedented population growth, unchecked industrial expansion and urbanization have diverted the human attention for ocean exploitation. Among its vast living resources, seaweeds are one of the best sources of food, fodder, fertilizer, medicine and chemicals. Seaweeds produce a varied and versatile biomass useful for multiple applications. They can be used in a broad variety of formats (e.g. fresh, dried, powder or flakes, salted, canned, liquid extracts or as prepared foods) for direct human consumption or processed into food additives and nutraceuticals, feeds, fertilizers, biofuels, cosmetics and medicines, amongst others. The macrophytic benthic marine algae, often called as seaweeds are used as food in Far East Countries since ancient times. According to FAO, over 30 countries around the world harvest annually about 3.8 million tones weight of seaweeds. Of this total, half of the quantity is utilised for human consumption and the rest for production of industrially important phycocolloids such as agar, carrageenan, and algin. The main types of edible seaweeds are Laminaria, Undaria, Porphyra and Monostroma. Almost all the edible seaweeds are cultivated on commercial scale especially in China, Japan and Korea to meet the market demands. The Porphyra cultivation in Japan is the Worldâ€™s biggest seaweed industry with a turnover of more than US $ 1.5 billion per annum.', '<p>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; font-size: 9pt; text-indent: -21.3pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[1].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; font-size: 9pt; text-indent: -21.3pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">Anis, M., Ahmed, S. &amp;Hasan, M. (2017). Algae as nutrition, medicine and cosmetic: the forgotten history, present status and future trend. World Journal of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences, 6: 1934&ndash;1959.</span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; font-size: 9pt; text-indent: -21.3pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[2].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; font-size: 9pt; text-indent: -21.3pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">ARPA-e. (2016). Macroalgae research inspiring novel energy resources (MARINER). U.S. Department of Energy. Available at https://arpa-e-foa.energy-gov.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[3].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">Balboa, E.M., Conde, E., Soto, M.L., P&eacute;rez-Armada, L. &amp;Dom&iacute;nguez, H. (2015). Cosmetics from marine sources. In Handbook of Marine Biotechnology (Kim, S.K., editor), 1015&ndash;1042. Springer, Berlin.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[4].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">Bjerregaard, R., Valderrama, D., Radulovich, R., Diana, J., Capron, M., Mckinnie, C.A., Cedric, M., Hopkins, K., Yarish, C., Goudey, C. &amp; Forster, J. (2016). Seaweed aquaculture for food security, income generation and environmental health in Tropical Developing Countries. World Bank Group, Washington, DC.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:21.3pt;mso-add-space:&#10;auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[5].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Buschmann, A.H., Gonzalez, M. del C.H. &amp; Varela, D. (2008). Seaweed future cultivation in Chile: perspectives and challenges. International Journal of Environment and Pollution, 33: 432&ndash;456.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:21.3pt;mso-add-space:&#10;auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[6].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Chapman, A.S., St&eacute;vant, P., Larssen, W.E., St&eacute;vant, P. &amp;Larssen, W.E. (2015). Food or fad? Challenges and opportunities for including seaweeds in a Nordic diet. Botanica Marina, 58: 423&ndash;433.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:21.3pt;mso-add-space:&#10;auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[7].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Chapman, V.J. and Chapman, D.J. 1980. Seaweeds and their uses. Published by Chapman and Hall, New York, USA. 334p.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:21.3pt;mso-add-space:&#10;auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[8].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Chopin, T., Buschmann, A.H., Halling, C., Troell, M., Kautsky, N., Neori, A., Kraemer, G.P., ZertucheGonz&aacute;lez, J.A., Yarish, C. &amp;Neefus, C. (2001). Integrating seaweeds into marine aquaculture systems: a key toward sustainability. Journal of Phycology, 37: 975&ndash;986.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:21.3pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[9].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Cornish, M., Critchley, A. &amp;Mouritsen, O. (2017). Consumption of seaweeds and the human brain. Journal of Applied Phycology. doi: 10.1007/s10811-016- 1049-3.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:&#10;Gautami;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:&#10;TE\">[10].De Silva, S.S. 1992. Tropical Mariculture. Academic&nbsp; &nbsp;Press, New York...</span></p>', 'Seaweeds, algae, phycocolloids, laminaria, biofuels, fertilizer', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr4104 Received : 21January, 2018 Accepted; 25February 2018 Available online : 18March 2018', 'Received: 21 January 2018 ; Accepted: 25 February 2018 ; Published: 18 March 2018', 1),
(79, 'Ethnomedicinal Practices in Different Communities of Telangana for Treatment of Wounds', 'Original Research Article I Volume 4 I Issue 1 I 2018', 'Vanga Sridhar, Tharigoppula Sunitha, Sriramula Harikishan Prasad, Bookya Padmaja', 'The American Journal Science and Medical Research; 4(1); 20-25', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr4105', '../pdffiles/cimg111556_41.5 sreedhar.vanga 20-25.pdf', 'India is well known for its great biological heritage and the present study is carried out in the Telangana State of India. The heavy greenery forests are home to several ethnic communities. The study was undertaken for the documentation of the traditional knowledge of ethnic people and to investigate plant distribution, abundance and biological activity of medicinal plants in the treatment of wounds. Field trips were made in Telangana districts to collect ethnomedicinal information from traditional healers. The collection of information was through interviews and during interviews plant details, part of the plant used, the method of preparation and dosage were recorded. The present study resulted in recording 99 medicinal plant species belonging to 54 families to treat different types of wounds by ethnic people in Telangana. The highest number of species belonging to Asteraceae (8 Species). Ethnomedicinal practices in the Telangana state of India revealed uses of 99 medicinal plants in the treatment of various types of wounds', '<p>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[1].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">AnkamSandhyarani (2017). Ethnobotanical study of medicinal plants used by traditional users in&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Kondagattu<b>. </b><i>The Ame J Sci&amp; Med Res</i>, 3(1):4-9.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[2].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Ayyanar M, Ignacimuthu S, (2009). Herbal medicines for wound healing among tribal people in Southern India: ethnobotanical and scientific evidences. <i>International Journal of Applied Research in Natural Products</i>, 2, 29&ndash;42.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&qu