ey of Antidiabetic plants used by tribes of Warangal District, Telangana State<b>. </b><i>The Ame J Sci&amp; Med Res</i>, 2(1):246-249.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[8].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Sandhya S, SaiKumar P, Vinod K.R, Banji D, Kumar K, (2011). Plantsaspotent antidiabetic andwoundhealingagents a review. <i>Hygeia, Journal of Drugs and Medicines</i>, 3, 11&ndash;19.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[9].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Strodtbeck F, (2001). Physiology of wound healing. <i>Newborn Infant Nursing Reviews,</i> 1, 43&ndash;51...<o:p></o:p></span></p>', 'thnomedicine, Wounds, Traditional healers, Telangana state.', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr4105 Received : 29January, 2018 Accepted; 12February 2018 Available online : 25March 2018', 'Received: 29 January 2018 ; Accepted: 12 February 2018 ; Published: 25 March 2018', 1),
(80, 'Evaluation of Oxidative DNA Damage in Gingival Epithelial Cells of Patients with Oral Sub Mucous Fibrosis', 'Original Research Article I Volume 4 I Issue 1 I 2018', 'V. Sreedevi, S. Sunayana Begum, M. Manjula', 'The American Journal Science and Medical Research; 4(1); 26-29', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr4106', '../pdffiles/cimg113252_41.6 sreedevi 26-29.pdf', 'Objective: The study was undertaken to determine oxidative DNA damage and free radical levels in patients with oral submucous fibrosis. Methods: The DNA damage was evaluated using comet assay and free radicals including nitric oxide and malondialdehyde levels were estimated using biochemical methods. Statistical analysis was performed using student t-test. Results: Comet assay revealed an increased frequency of comets in patients when compared to controls. The mean levels of nitric oxide and lipid peroxidation were significantly increased in patients when compared to controls. ', '<p>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[1].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">Cox SC, Walker DM. Oral submucous fibrosis. A review. Australian Dental Journal 1996; 41(5): 294-&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;299.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:norma