a&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[11].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">Tata,J.R.1970. Regulation of protein synthesis by growth and developmental hormones. In: Biochemical Actions of Hormones, (ed.) G. Litwack, Academic press, New York, pp. 89-133.</span></p>\r\n<!--[if supportFields]><b style=\'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\'><span lang=EN-IN\r\nstyle=\'font-size:9.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:\"Book Antiqua\",\"serif\";\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\nGautami;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:\r\nTE\'><span style=\'mso-element:field-end\'></span></span></b><![endif]-->  <!--[if supportFields]><b style=\'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\'><span lang=EN-IN\r\nstyle=\'font-size:9.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:\"Book Antiqua\",\"serif\";\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\nGautami;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:\r\nTE\'><span style=\'mso-element:field-end\'></span></span></b><![endif]-->', 'Thyroxine; Skeletal Muscle Protein; RNA;Anabas testudineus', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr421 Received : 3 March, 2018 Accepted; 18April, 2018 Available online :22 April, 2018', 'Received: 3 March 2018 ; Accepted: 18 April 2018 ; Published: 22 April 2018', 1),
(82, 'Studies on the diversity of butterflies in and around the Nizam College, Hyderabad, Telangana State, India', 'Original Research Article I Volume 4 I Issue 2 I 2018', 'Madhavi. M, Krishna', 'The American Journal of Science and Medical Research; 4(2); 4-9', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr422', '../pdffiles/cimg044817_42.2 madhavi 4-9.pdf', 'Butterflies are one of the most important assemblages of insects that act as biodiversity indicators as well as natureâ€™s gardeners. Owing to habitat destruction for developmental activities in urban environment and unscientific management of natural resources, much of our native butterflies are fast disappearing and at present, their survival is under threat. The objective of the present survey is focused on the assessment of the diversity and seasonal abundance of butterfly with vegetation composition of habitat and conservation priorities in the study area. A total of 4 species of butterflies were recorded during August-2017to March-2018.This study is aimed towards contributing to the plan of biodiversity restoration in our campus and development of management strategies so as to ensure sustenance of butterflies and ecosystem services derived from them.', '<p>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[1].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">Alaruikka,D; Kotze, D.J; Matveinen, K and Niemel&auml;, J (2002). &lsquo;Carabid Beetle and Spider Assemblages along a Forested Urban&ndash;Rural Gradient in Southern Finland&rsquo;. <i>Journal of Insect Conservation, </i>6:195-206.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[2].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Allred, H.A (1975) &lsquo;Arachnids as Ecological Indicators&rsquo;. <i>Great Basin Naturalist,</i> 35: 405- 406.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[3].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settin