quot;\">Clergeau,P; Savard,J.P.L; Mennechez,G and Falardeau,G. (1998). &lsquo;Bird Abundance and Diversity along an Urban-rural Gradient: A Comparative Study of Two Cities on Different Continents&rsquo;. <i>The Condor: An International Journal of Avian Biology</i>, 100: 413-425.<i><o:p></o:p></i></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[10].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Hager, H.A. (1998). &lsquo;Environmental Effects of Heavy Spillage from a Destroyed Pesticide Store near Hargeisa (Somaliland) Assessed during the Dry Season, Using Reptiles and Amphibians as Bioindicators&rsquo;. <i>Ecoscience</i>5: 139-147...<o:p></o:p></span></p>', 'Butterfly, species diversity, distance transect method, Nizam College ', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr422 Received :9March, 2018 Accepted; 19April, 2018 Available online :28April, 2018', 'Received: 19 August 2018 ; Accepted: 23 September 2018 ; Published: 29 September 2018', 1),
(85, 'Synthesis of Thiosemicarbazones Derivatives and their in vitro Antioxidant Activity', 'Original Research Article I Volume 4 I Issue 3 I 2018', 'Laxmi Manasa Chilakamari', 'The American Journal of Science and Medical Research; 4(3); 12-15', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr433', '../pdffiles/cimg051129_43.3 laxmi manasa 12-15.pdf', 'Thiosemicarbazones were reported to have antineoplastic, antibacterial, antiviral, antifungal, antimalarial, nueroprotective, antitubercular activities. This study aimed to synthesis of Thiosemicarbazones and evaluation for its antioxidant activities.The two derivatives of thiosemicarbazones are synthesized by using a conventional one step processes in which the respective halo-substituted acetophenones are condensed with thiosemicarbazide to result in the formation of the product.The structures of thiosemicarbazones were confirmed by spectroscopic (IR, 1H NMR, 13C NMR and MS) method. The antioxidant activity of these thiosemicarbazones was evaluated, in vitro and itâ€™s shown that some of these compounds had significant antioxidant activity.', '<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[1].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -21.3pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">D. L. Klayman, J.P Scovill, J.F. Barosevich and C.J. Mason, J.Med. Chem., 1979, 22, 1367-1373.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\" style=\"margin-left:21.3pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:&#10;-21.3pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\">