-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">Rao KP. Some aspects of the biochemical basis of metabolic adaptation. Helgoland Mar. Res., 1966. 14(1-4): 439 &ndash; 450.<b><o:p></o:p></b></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;&#10;tab-stops:124.0pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\">10.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">Lang F, Busch G L, Ritter M, V&ouml;lkl H, Waldegger S, Gulbins E, H&auml;ussinger D. Functional significance of cell volume regulatory mechanisms. Physiol. Rev., 1998.&nbsp; 78: 247 &ndash; 306.&nbsp;<b><o:p></o:p></b></span></p>', 'Barytelphusa guerini, Temperature, Protein, Carbohydrate, Muscle and  Hepatopancreas', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr512 Received :29 December, 2018 Accepted; 2February, 2019 Available online :12 February, 2019', 'Received: 29 December 2018 ; Accepted: 2 February 2019 ; Published: 12 February 2019', 1),
(93, 'In Vitro Screening of 20 Indian Medicinal Plants for their Anti-Cholinesterase Effects', 'Original Research Article I Volume 5 I Issue 2 I 2019', 'D.Sripriya, T. Suvarna', 'The American Journal of Science and Medical Research; 5(2); 1-5', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr521', '../pdffiles/cimg070720_51.2 sunitha 6-9.pdf', 'The purpose of the present study is to contribute to an understanding of the actual and potential role of  20 traditional medicinal plants based Methanol  extracts role in the Enzyme inhibition Assays against  Alzheimerâ€™s disease. The objective of the study was to investigate the Acetyl cholinesterase Enzyme inhibitory activity of 90% methanol extracts of 20 selected medicinal plants. Quantitative Analysis made with the help of 96 wells Micro plate technique. Readings have been done with the help of Micro plate reader. Calculation of IC-50 Values by interpolation of a RIA (or) ELISA interpolates unknowns from sigmoid curve using Graph Pad PRISM2.8.1.1 (330) Software. Comparison of IC50 Values with standard. In the present study, methanol extracts of 20 plants used in Indian Ayurvedic system of medicine for improving cognitive function were screened for acetyl cholinesterase inhibitory activity by Ell manâ€™s micro plate calorimetric method against Alzheimerâ€™s disease.  ', '<p>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -14.2pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -14.2pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">Ellman G. L., Courtney K. D., Andres V., Jr., Featherstone R. M. A new and rapid colorimetric&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;determination of acetylcholinesterase activity. Biochemical Pharmacology. 1961;7(2):88&ndash;95. doi:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 10.1016/0006-2952(61)90145-9. [PubMed] [CrossRef] [Google Scholar]</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:14.2pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-14.2pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Stedman, E., Stedman, E., Easson, L.H.: Choline-esterase. An enzyme present in the blood-serum of the horse. Biochem. J. 26(6), 2056 (1932) Cross Ref. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:14.2pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-14.2pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&q