an&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Yakawa T. and Pitt J.M., 1985. <i>Nematode storage and transport.</i> PCT/AU 85/ 00020. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:21.3pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-21.3pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;&#10;tab-stops:355.5pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[11].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Nickle, W. R. and Shapiro, M. 1992. <i>Use of a stilbene brightener Tinopal LPW, as a radiation protectant for Steinernemacorpocapsae</i>. Journal of Nematology, 24 (3): 371-373.<o:p></o:p></span></p>', 'Adjuvants; Spodopteralitura; Glycerin; UV protector; Sodium bicarbonate', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr531 Received :2 July 2019 Accepted; 25 August 2019 Available online : 19 September 2019', 'Received: 2 July 2019 ; Accepted: 25 August 2019 ; Published: 19 September 2019', 1);
INSERT INTO `ajsmr_abstracts` (`contentid`, `conttitle`, `issuedetails`, `authors`, `journal`, `doi`, `abstract`, `abstractsdesc`, `referencestxt`, `keywords`, `howtoguide`, `articledates`, `status`) VALUES
(95, 'In silico Molecular Docking Studies of compounds from Rumex vesicarius against Pancreatic Î±-Amylase', 'Original Research Article I Volume 5 I Issue 4 I 2019', 'Rakesh Davella and Estari Mamidala', 'The American Journal Science and Medical Research; 5(4); 1-10', 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7188942', '../pdffiles/cimg081300_10.17812_ajsmr541.pdf', 'In spite of the global occurrence of type-2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM) infection and lack of auspicious treatment for Diabetes patients, there are only a few drugs accepted for the managing of infected patients. There is an urgent need to discover newer anti-diabetic drugs with novel mechanism of action and with efforts to reduce attrition rate in early drug discovery stages. The objective of this study is the evaluation of Rumex vesicarius compounds for anti-T2DM activity. In silico anti-T2DM lead prioritization was performed on a set of known compounds from R. vesicarius medicinal plant. The energy minimized structures of these molecules were docked into Pancreatic Î±-Amylase. Docking experiments were done using Autodock software for seven compounds docking with Î±-Amylase. Rhein was found to be a lead with better docking scores. The results showed that there is scope for the improvement of activity of Isovitexin analogs to discover a potent anti-T2DM compound.', '<p>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -27pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[1].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -27pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">S. Ramachandran, A. Rajasekaran, and N. Adhirajan, &ldquo;In vivo and in vitro antidiabetic activity of Terminalia paniculata bark: an evaluation of possible phytoconstituents and mechanisms for blood glucose control in diabetes,&rdquo; ISRN Pharmacology, vol. 2013, Article ID 484675, 10 pages, 2013.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:27.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-27.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[2].<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">B. A. Sheikh, L. Pari, A. Rathinam, and R. Chandramohan, &ldquo;Trans-anethole, a terpenoid ameliorates hyperglycemia by regulating key enzymes of carbohydrate metabolism in streptozotocin induced diabetic rats,&rdquo; Biochimie, vol. 112, pp. 57&ndash;65, 2015.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:27.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-27.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&qu