bottom:10.0pt;margin-left:22.5pt;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;&#10;text-indent:-22.5pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:35.45pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[9]<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Mazon, Af.,Monteiro, Eas., Pinheiro, Ghd. and Fernandes, Mn.: Brazilian Journal of Biology, vol. 62, no. 4A, p. 621-631 (2002).<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:10.0pt;margin-left:22.5pt;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;&#10;text-indent:-22.5pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:35.45pt\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[10]<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Fernandes, Mn. And Mazon, F.:Enfield: Science Publishers, p. 203-231 (2003).<o:p></o:p></span></p>', 'Sonata, Hypertrophy, Hyperplasia, Epithilial lifting, Pyknotic nuclei, Gliosis', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr631 Received : 12July, 2020 Accepted; 22August, 2020 Available online :29 August, 2020', 'Received: 12 July 2020;; Accepted: 22 August 2020;; Published: 29 August 2020', 1),
(99, 'Physicochemical Properties of Termite Mounds and Surrounding Soils in Kothaguda Forest Region, Mahabubabad District, Telangana', 'Original Research Article I Volume 6 I Issue 4 I 2020', 'Mamatha G and Narayana E', 'The American Journal of Science and Medical Research', 'http://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr641', '../pdffiles/cimg090526_64.1 Narayana 1-61.pdf', 'Physicochemical analysis of termite mounds and surrounding soils in Kothaguda forest region were investigated during June, 2018 to May, 2019. The test parameters such as soil pá´´, organic carbon, available nitrogen, available phosphorus and available potassium were determined in mounds soil and surrounding soils. These parameters were increased in mounds soil than surrounding earth soil in rainy season followed by winter and summer seasons. Elemental analysis shows significant variability of the elemental ranging about soil pá´´ (7.32-8.18), EC (0.09-0.36ds/m), OC (0.78-1.90%), AN (75kg / ha to 414 kg/ha), AP (66 to 328 kg/ha), APo (288 to 367 kg / ha) in mound soil followed by pá´´(6.34-7.2),EC(0.06-0.27ds/m), OC(0.64-1.79%),AN(125-351kg/ha),AP(66-328kg/ha), and Apo(201-365kg/ha) in surrounding soils during rainy season. During winter season, the elements ranged about pá´´ (6.05-7.87), EC (0.11- 0.79dS/m), OC (0.53-1.08%), AN (125kg / ha to 238kg/ha), AP (10.26 to 41 kg/ha), APo (149 to 249kg / ha) in mound soil followed by pá´´(5.5-8.13), EC(0.05-0.72 dS/m), OC(0.31 â€“ 1.04%), AN(88-226kg/ha),AP(10.26 - 39kg/ha), and Apo(149 â€“ 286 kg/ha) in surrounding soils respectively. In summer season, the elemental analysis were recorded about pá´´ (5.72-7.69), EC (0.12- 0.78dS/m), OC (0.44-1.01%), AN (89kg / ha to 218 kg/ha), AP (9.20 to 25 kg/ha), APo (116 to 200kg / ha) in mound soil followed by pá´´(5.07-7.82), EC(0.05-0.71dS/m), OC(0.30 â€“ 1.02%), AN(50 - 216kg/ha), AP(9.20 - 37kg/ha), and Apo(101 â€“ 279 kg/ha) in surrounding soils respectively. The results show that all the test parameters were higher in mounds soil than the surrounding soils. However, the available potassium was higher in the surrounding soils. From the current study, it can be concluded that the physicochemical properties of mounds soil were very high and influenced the plant growth in the mounds area when compared to non-mound areas.', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;<span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -22.5pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[1]<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -22.5pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">Dawes T. Z. (2010). Re-establishment ecological functioning by Mulching and Termite Invasion in a&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;degraded soil in an Australian savanna. Soil Biology and Biochemistry 42:1825-1834</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:&#10;9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[2]<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Radojevic, M. and Bashkin, V.N. (2005). &ldquo;Practiced Environmental Analysis Royal Society of&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ChemistryCambridge P. 78. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:&#10;9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[3]<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">Ayininuola, G.M: &quot;Variability in geochemical properties of Termitaris (2009). University of a Ibadan case study&quot;. American Journal of primatology 69 (7): 567-575.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNoSpacing\" style=\"margin-left: 22.5pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -22.5pt;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:&#10;9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;\">[4]<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"f