i>. Ecotoxicology and Environmental Safety </i>50: 203&ndash;216<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:27.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-27.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;color:#231F20\">[9]<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;&#10;color:#231F20\">Modra H, Svobodova Z, Kolafova J. 1998. Comparison of differential leukocyte counts in fish of economic and indicator importance. <i>ActaVeterinaria Brno </i>67: 215&ndash;226.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:27.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-27.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;;&#10;color:#231F20\">[10]<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;&#10;font-family:&quot;Book Antiqua&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;&#10;color:#231F20\">Nwani CD, Mkpadobi BN, Onyishi G, Echi PC, Chukwuka CO, Olua SN, Ivoke N. 2014. Changes in behavior and hematological parameters of freshwater African catfish <i>Clariasgariepinus</i>(Burchell 1822) following sublethal exposure to chloramphenicol. <i>Drug and Chemical Toxicology </i>37: 107&ndash;130...<o:p></o:p></span></p>', 'Haemotology, C. carpio, Acute toxicity, WBC, RBC', 'https://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr.2021.721 Received: 2 April 2021; Accepted: 21 May 2021 Published: 4 June 2021', 'Received: 2 April 2021; Accepted: 21 May 2021 ; Published: 4 June 2021', 1);
INSERT INTO `ajsmr_abstracts` (`contentid`, `conttitle`, `issuedetails`, `authors`, `journal`, `doi`, `abstract`, `abstractsdesc`, `referencestxt`, `keywords`, `howtoguide`, `articledates`, `status`) VALUES
(102, 'Assessment of insecticide, lesenta toxicity on antioxidant enzymes in common carp (Cyprinus carpio L.)', 'Original Research Article I Volume 7 I Issue 3 I 2021', 'Mummadi Narsing Rao and R.P. Mali', 'The American Journal of Science and Medical Research', 'https://dx.doi.org/10.17812/ajsmr.2021.731', '../pdffiles/cimg095810_73.1 NARSING 1-4.pdf', 'Indiscriminate discharge of pharmaceutical waste into the aquatic ecosystem may pose major health challenges to aquatic biota. The effect of acute exposure to ibuprofen was studied utilizing changes in haematological parameters under static bio-assay method in common carp (Cyprinus carpio). For this investigation, the fishes are split into four separate groups. Based on the sub-lethal toxicity research, fishes exposed to 1/10th of LC50 value of ibuprofen. The 96-h LC50 of Ibuprofen was 12.75 mg/L. in C. carpio. Therefore, for this experiment, fish were subjected to 0.25, 0.50 and 1 mg/L doses of ibuprofen. At the end of each exposure session (7th day, 14th day and 21st day), fish specimens were anesthetised with tricaine methane sulfonate to permit the collection of blood samples. The RBC count in group IV fishes of ibuprofen treated fishes, at 21 day of exposure, was lowered and it is statistically significant (p<0.01) to control fishes. WBC counts in fishes that had 7 and 14 days exposure to ibuprofen were not statistically altered, compared to control rats. Ibuprofen treated fish did not elicit any significant alterations (p Ëƒ 0.05) with reference to monocytes, basophils and eosinophils. Based on the above results, it might be inferred that administration of ibuprofen, may elicit immunological perturbations, and their toxicity may rise depending on the dose.', '<p>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -22.5pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[1]<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -22.5pt; font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">Isani G., Monari M., Andreani G., Fabbri M and Carpen&egrave; E (2003). Effect of copper exposure on the antioxidant enzymes in bivalve mollusk Scapharca inaequivalvis. Veterinary Research Communications, 27(1): 691-693</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:22.5pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-22.5pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">[2]<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: &quot;Book Antiqua&quot;, &quot;serif&quot;;\">Isla MI., Moreno MIN., Sampietro AR and Vattuone MA (2001). Antioxidant activity of Argentine propolis extracts. Journal of Ethnopharmacology, Lausanne, 76(2): 165-170.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;&#10;margin-bottom:0in;margin-left:22.5pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;&#10;text-align:justify;text-indent:-22.5pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!