t based virtual screening. Bioorganic &amp; Medicinal Chemistry Letters, 2014. 24(22): p. 5251-5255.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:13.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;color:#595959;mso-themecolor:text1;mso-themetint:&#10;166;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-bidi-language:TE\">Sengupta, S., et al., In-Silico Modelling of 1-3-[3-(Substituted Phenyl) Prop-2-Enoyl) Phenyl Thiourea Against Anti-Inflammatory Drug Targets. Biosciences Biotechnology Research Asia, 2021. 18(2): p. 413.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:13.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;color:#595959;mso-themecolor:text1;mso-themetint:&#10;166;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-bidi-language:TE\">Boyanovsky, B.B. and N.R. Webb, Biology of Secretory Phospholipase A2. Cardiovascular Drugs and Therapy, 2008. 23(1).<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:13.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;color:#595959;mso-themecolor:text1;mso-themetint:&#10;166;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-bidi-language:TE\">Triggiani, M., et al., Secretory phospholipases A2 in inflammatory and allergic diseases: not just enzymes. Journal of Allergy and Clinical Immunology, 2005. 116(5): p. 1000-1006.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:13.0pt;font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;color:#595959;mso-themecolor:text1;mso-themetint:&#10;166;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-bidi-language:TE\">Dennis, E.A. and P.C. Norris, Eicosanoid storm in infection and inflammation. Nature Reviews Immunology, 2015. 15(8): p. 511-523.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justif